==============================================================================
(1) log|2 cos pi t| = log|2 sin 2 pi t| - log|2 sin pi t| ?
==============================================================================
  max |lhs - rhs| over 200001 points, poles excluded: 1.776e-15
  so X = -log|cos pi t| = log 2 - (T_2 - 1) log|2 sin|, with T_2 f(t) = f(2t).
  On the chi-component T_2 has eigenvalue chi(2) (a -> 2a permutes the units),
  so (1 - T_2) contributes exactly the factor (1 - chi(2)) of prop:chardecomp.
  CONCLUSION: prop:chardecomp is Dirichlet's classical evaluation of
  sum chi(a) log|2 sin(pi a/f)| transported by the double-angle formula.

